WEBVTT

00:00:01.158 --> 00:00:01.908
[PHOENIX]
My name is Phoenix Wright,

00:00:01.991 --> 00:00:03.325
and I'm a defense attorney.

00:00:03.408 --> 00:00:05.200
I've made a pledge to
stand up for those who have

00:00:05.283 --> 00:00:07.116
no one else in their corner.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.783
No matter how
tough the case may be,

00:00:08.866 --> 00:00:10.950
or how high the odds
are stacked against us.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.908
I'll do whatever it takes
to fight for the truth!

00:00:13.991 --> 00:00:15.658
But of course,
there was a time before I made

00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:18.283
that pledge and earned
my attorney's badge.

00:00:18.366 --> 00:00:19.825
Five years ago,
something changed

00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:21.741
the direction of my life
and convinced me

00:00:21.825 --> 00:00:23.658
to be a voice for justice!

00:00:29.991 --> 00:00:32.158
[DOUG] Listen, man.
You should stop seeing her.

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:33.616
[PHOENIX]
What? How is our relationship

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.033
any of your business?

00:00:35.116 --> 00:00:36.658
[thunder rumbles]

00:00:36.741 --> 00:00:38.866
Please. This is
for your own sake.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.033
She's bad news,
and that's putting it lightly.

00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:42.825
[PHOENIX growls]
You're lying!

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:44.825
[DOUG] There's something
you need to know about her.

00:00:44.908 --> 00:00:46.200
Before you get hurt.

00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:49.408
[thunder rumbles]

00:00:49.491 --> 00:00:50.533
[PHOENIX]
Shut your mouth!

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:52.700
She's not like that!
There's no way!

00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:53.991
[blow lands]

00:01:01.241 --> 00:01:04.033
[PHOENIX]
No. It's not my fault.

00:01:04.116 --> 00:01:06.366
It... couldn't be.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.241
I didn't kill this guy!

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.075
[thunder cracks

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.991
[MIA]
Ugh. It's almost time.

00:02:57.075 --> 00:02:58.950
I can't believe
how nervous I am.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.408
[MARVIN clears throat]

00:03:05.491 --> 00:03:08.908
[MIA yelps]
You startled me, Mr. Grossberg!

00:03:08.991 --> 00:03:10.491
Good morning!

00:03:10.575 --> 00:03:13.533
Now, now, Mia.
There's no need to be so jumpy.

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:15.616
You might get questioned
for suspicious behavior.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.658
I'm perfectly calm, thank you.

00:03:17.741 --> 00:03:19.158
Is this not the face
of tranquility?!

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:22.408
--Uh... Ms. Fey! [coughs]
--Please forgive my outburst.

00:03:22.491 --> 00:03:25.491
I understand the emotion,
but no more manhandling!

00:03:25.575 --> 00:03:28.616
[sighs] Your first time
trying a case, eh?

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.450
I, Marvin Grossberg,
vow to be your rock.

00:03:31.533 --> 00:03:32.616
Actually, to be clear,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.408
this'll be my second
time to try a case.

00:03:34.491 --> 00:03:36.616
Nevertheless,
you gave me quite a surprise.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.991
What made you come to me
all fiery eyed last night

00:03:39.075 --> 00:03:40.700
and insist on handling this?

00:03:40.783 --> 00:03:44.116
When I heard about it yesterday,
it caught my interest.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.491
[MIA] The defendant's name
is Phoenix Wright.

00:03:46.575 --> 00:03:47.950
He's accused of murder,

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.866
and the official cause of
death was electrocution.

00:03:52.241 --> 00:03:53.408
[MARVIN]
And here he is.

00:03:53.491 --> 00:03:55.033
This is Phoenix Wright.

00:03:55.116 --> 00:03:58.033
The man whose freedom you
will be fighting for today.

00:03:58.116 --> 00:04:00.158
[PHOENIX] Thanks so much
for taking my case!

00:04:00.241 --> 00:04:01.658
I know you can clear my name!

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.533
I'll help you anyway I can!

00:04:03.616 --> 00:04:04.866
[coughs]

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.366
Yes, of course. Thank you.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:08.158
Mister Wry!

00:04:08.241 --> 00:04:09.241
[PHOENIX]
Great!

00:04:10.741 --> 00:04:12.075
[PHOENIX]
Oh, but my name.

00:04:12.158 --> 00:04:14.116
It's Wright, like
the flying brothers.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.241
I misspoke, Mr. Wright!
It won't happen again!

00:04:17.325 --> 00:04:19.033
I swear on my life
I won't fail you!

00:04:19.116 --> 00:04:20.325
[coughs]

00:04:20.408 --> 00:04:22.366
Forgive me.

00:04:25.533 --> 00:04:27.158
[PHOENIX] All I want is
to prove my innocence,

00:04:27.241 --> 00:04:29.241
because I would
never kill anybody!

00:04:29.325 --> 00:04:30.991
[MIA] I need to keep
things in perspective,

00:04:31.075 --> 00:04:33.075
he's got every right
to be nervous.

00:04:33.158 --> 00:04:35.450
Come on, Mia. Stay strong!

00:04:35.533 --> 00:04:36.866
My first trial, a year ago,

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.450
was such a
traumatizing experience.

00:04:39.533 --> 00:04:43.533
I thought I'd never set
foot inside a courtroom again.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.700
But I can't keep running away.

00:04:45.783 --> 00:04:48.325
I have to go back
and face my fears.

00:04:48.408 --> 00:04:49.491
And this time...

00:04:49.575 --> 00:04:51.366
...I believe in myself.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.450
I'm gonna win this!

00:04:53.533 --> 00:04:59.033
[CROWD murmuring]

00:04:59.116 --> 00:05:00.450
Order, please!

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.950
This court is hereby in session
to hear the murder trial

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.491
of Mister Phoenix Wright.

00:05:04.575 --> 00:05:07.283
The defense team is
ready to begin, Your Honor.

00:05:07.366 --> 00:05:10.533
Yes, Your Honor. The
prosecution is ready as well.

00:05:10.616 --> 00:05:12.533
Ms. Fey. Am I to understand

00:05:12.616 --> 00:05:14.325
that you'll be
leading the defense?

00:05:14.408 --> 00:05:16.866
Um... Yes. Is there a problem?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.491
No, but I was under the
impression Mister Grossberg

00:05:19.575 --> 00:05:21.200
would be fulfilling
duties of council.

00:05:21.283 --> 00:05:24.158
Oh. Well... Mister Grossberg
had an urgent matter

00:05:24.241 --> 00:05:25.825
that came up all of a sudden.

00:05:25.908 --> 00:05:27.658
So I'm here in his
stead, Your Honor.

00:05:27.741 --> 00:05:28.825
Is that the case?

00:05:28.908 --> 00:05:30.491
Because that man
standing next to you looks

00:05:30.575 --> 00:05:32.325
a lot like him, Ms. Fey.

00:05:32.408 --> 00:05:33.783
That's true.

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.325
It turns out the urgent
matter was that

00:05:35.408 --> 00:05:37.700
I desperately needed to
observe this trial, Your Honor.

00:05:37.783 --> 00:05:38.575
[MIA]
Mm-hmm.

00:05:38.658 --> 00:05:39.575
[JUDGE]
Hmmmm.

00:05:39.658 --> 00:05:40.991
[CROWD murmuring]

00:05:41.075 --> 00:05:42.325
[JUDGE]
Well then.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.950
Mister Payne, proceed with
your opening statement.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.116
[PAYNE]
Hmm. It boggles the mind.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.950
To think they would send
someone so green to go

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:50.116
against a "rookie
killer" like me.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.616
[MIA growls]

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.575
[PAYNE] Anyway, I'd like to
proceed with a brief summary

00:05:53.658 --> 00:05:55.241
of the events in question.

00:05:55.325 --> 00:05:57.866
This tragic incident
occurred one rainy afternoon,

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.658
on the local campus
of Ivy University.

00:06:00.741 --> 00:06:03.200
The victim of this
horrific crime was Doug Swallow,

00:06:03.283 --> 00:06:06.116
a senior so close to finishing
his pharmacology degree.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.575
[JUDGE]
Pharmacology.

00:06:07.658 --> 00:06:09.158
[PAYNE] Some fellow students
discovered the crime scene

00:06:09.241 --> 00:06:10.491
and notified the authorities.

00:06:10.575 --> 00:06:12.866
They found Mr. Swallow's
body, and the defendant

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:16.033
who'd made a complete
mess of his get-away attempt.

00:06:16.116 --> 00:06:18.575
Phoenix Wright sits before us.

00:06:18.658 --> 00:06:20.658
Wright is a third-year
Ivy University student

00:06:20.741 --> 00:06:23.325
who is pursuing a degree
in the arts, of all things.

00:06:23.408 --> 00:06:25.366
Apparently, this man
and the late Mister Swallow

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.616
had some bad blood
between the two of them.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.200
Please elaborate.

00:06:29.283 --> 00:06:31.366
[PHOENIX] You make it sound like
there was some big feud, but...

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:32.991
[coughs]

00:06:33.075 --> 00:06:35.825
[JUDGE] Contain your coughing
or we'll be forced to eject you.

00:06:35.908 --> 00:06:37.408
[CROWD murmurin]

00:06:37.491 --> 00:06:38.866
But there was a disagreement

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.783
between the two men.
Wasn't there, young lady?

00:06:41.866 --> 00:06:42.741
[MIA gasps]

00:06:42.825 --> 00:06:44.116
Nothing to say?

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.658
[chuckles] If you call yourself
a defense attorney,

00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:49.283
surely, you must know all
about what went down.

00:06:49.366 --> 00:06:52.658
[MIA] So. He wants to
test me, does he? Fine.

00:06:52.741 --> 00:06:54.200
I'm not scared of Payne.

00:06:55.366 --> 00:06:57.408
I assume this so-called
"bad blood" you mention

00:06:57.491 --> 00:06:59.908
has to do with Dahlia Hawthorne?

00:06:59.991 --> 00:07:01.866
[JUDGE]
And who might that be?

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.616
[PAYNE] Currently, the
defendant's girlfriend.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.658
But until half a year ago,
Miss Hawthorne could usually be

00:07:07.741 --> 00:07:10.325
found hanging on the arm of
the victim, Mister Swallow

00:07:10.408 --> 00:07:12.700
I'm sure that romantic
entanglement was the motive

00:07:12.783 --> 00:07:14.408
behind this senseless murder.

00:07:14.491 --> 00:07:17.825
[JUDGE] Hmm. So it was your
run-of-the mill love triangle.

00:07:17.908 --> 00:07:19.116
[PHOENIX]
I object!

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.241
You'd better keep my
sweet Dollie out of this!

00:07:21.325 --> 00:07:22.533
--[JUDGE] Hmm?
--[PHOENIX] You hear me?

00:07:22.616 --> 00:07:23.908
[PAYNE] Please take
another look at the victim

00:07:23.991 --> 00:07:25.700
in the crime scene photo.

00:07:25.783 --> 00:07:26.950
[gasping]

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:28.908
[JUDGE] Hm. Is he
holding a medicine bottle?

00:07:28.991 --> 00:07:31.241
[PAYNE]
Indeed. It's Coldkiller Z,

00:07:31.325 --> 00:07:33.783
an elixir that claims
it "kills colds dead."

00:07:33.866 --> 00:07:35.908
[PHOENIX]
Hey, wait a second, that's mine!

00:07:35.991 --> 00:07:37.616
I'd been trying to
kill this cold with it,

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.491
but I ended up losing the
bottle somewhere that day.

00:07:40.575 --> 00:07:43.408
I could swear I had it
on me till lunchtime, at least.

00:07:43.491 --> 00:07:45.366
[JUDGE]
Defendant! Control yourself!

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.450
[PHOENIX]
I'm sorry, sir.

00:07:46.533 --> 00:07:47.866
[MIA]
He behaves like a child.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:50.158
[PAYNE] Your Honor.
The defendant's fingerprints

00:07:50.241 --> 00:07:52.783
were found all over the bottle,
so he's telling the truth.

00:07:52.866 --> 00:07:54.700
Mere moments
before his untimely death,

00:07:54.783 --> 00:07:56.366
the victim used the last
bit of his strength

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.075
he could muster to wrest it
from the hands of his attacker.

00:07:59.158 --> 00:08:00.533
All to ensure
that the killer would be

00:08:00.616 --> 00:08:03.033
identified as Phoenix Wright!

00:08:03.116 --> 00:08:04.950
[PHOENIX yells]

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.575
His argument
carries incredible force!

00:08:07.658 --> 00:08:09.491
Another thing I'd
like to mention is the watch

00:08:09.575 --> 00:08:12.241
pictured here on the
victim's wrist is broken.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.658
[JUDGE]
Is that so?

00:08:13.741 --> 00:08:15.033
[PAYNE]
The impact from the death-blow

00:08:15.116 --> 00:08:17.366
is what likely
caused it to break.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.450
So we can take that to
mean the time of the murder

00:08:19.533 --> 00:08:21.908
was exactly 3:05 PM.

00:08:21.991 --> 00:08:24.783
Let us proceed to the
defendant's cross-examination.

00:08:24.866 --> 00:08:26.825
State your name and occupation.

00:08:26.908 --> 00:08:29.033
[PHOENIX] Gladly! My
name is Phoenix Wright!

00:08:29.116 --> 00:08:33.658
My occupation is,
uh, accused murderer?

00:08:33.741 --> 00:08:35.783
What did you do
before you were arrested?!

00:08:35.866 --> 00:08:37.950
[PHOENIX]
Oh. I'm a college student!

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.491
[JUDGE] Mister Wright,
please tell the court

00:08:39.575 --> 00:08:41.700
about the events of said day.

00:08:44.366 --> 00:08:46.200
[PHOENIX] That morning,
Doug had asked me to meet him

00:08:46.283 --> 00:08:50.283
behind the Pharmacology
Department at 2:45 PM.

00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:53.575
We talked for a bit and then
parted ways around 3.

00:08:53.658 --> 00:08:56.366
So, had you and the victim
had any previous interactions?

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:57.866
[PHOENIX]
Never. That was the first time

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.450
we'd spoken to each other.

00:08:59.533 --> 00:09:01.783
He said he wanted to
talk to me about Dollie.

00:09:01.866 --> 00:09:04.116
Dahlia Hawthorne. Right, Wright?

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.158
[PHOENIX]
Yes, Dollie, my soulmate!

00:09:06.241 --> 00:09:08.700
This sweater I'm wearing
is a token of our love.

00:09:08.783 --> 00:09:10.741
And she gave me
this beautiful pendant!

00:09:10.825 --> 00:09:13.158
Before I met him,
she and I had lunch together!

00:09:13.241 --> 00:09:14.991
She made omelets and
it was just like eating

00:09:15.075 --> 00:09:16.325
a little bite of Heaven!

00:09:16.408 --> 00:09:18.491
You testified that you
and the victim had a talk.

00:09:18.575 --> 00:09:20.200
Was that really
all that happened?

00:09:20.283 --> 00:09:21.950
[PHOENIX]
Uh, what do you mean by that?

00:09:22.033 --> 00:09:24.033
Did the situation
get heated and escalate

00:09:24.116 --> 00:09:27.325
into something physical?
Like shoving?

00:09:27.408 --> 00:09:29.283
[PHOENIX] No way, I'm just
not that kind of person,

00:09:29.366 --> 00:09:30.825
I would never lay
a finger on the guy!

00:09:30.908 --> 00:09:31.908
[PAYNE]
Objection!

00:09:31.991 --> 00:09:33.241
Please, Your Honor.

00:09:33.325 --> 00:09:35.825
Go and take another look
at the crime scene photo.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:38.658
You can see the victim
was wearing a leather jacket.

00:09:38.741 --> 00:09:41.116
Upon further inspection,
we found the defendant's

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.158
palm print on the left breast.

00:09:43.241 --> 00:09:45.158
It's there, clear as day.

00:09:45.241 --> 00:09:46.408
[MIA gasps]

00:09:46.491 --> 00:09:48.408
Obviously, Mister Wright,
your testimony

00:09:48.491 --> 00:09:50.116
to the court is full of lies!

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.450
[yells, coughs]

00:09:52.533 --> 00:09:54.533
Well, Wright,
what do you have to say?

00:09:54.616 --> 00:09:56.033
[PHOENIX]
That's exactly what happened!

00:09:56.116 --> 00:09:59.200
I'm so sorry!
I really did shove him!

00:09:59.283 --> 00:10:00.408
[CROWD gasping, murmurin]

00:10:00.491 --> 00:10:02.366
[JUDGE] Order in the court!
Order, please!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.283
I'm shocked. This is
the first I've heard of it.

00:10:04.366 --> 00:10:07.283
We're done, Mia. Might
as well stick a big fork in us.

00:10:07.366 --> 00:10:09.491
Not yet. I can't
just let it end like this.

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:11.450
I can think of only one
way the defendant could have

00:10:11.533 --> 00:10:13.741
left such an
unmistakable hand print.

00:10:13.825 --> 00:10:16.283
He assaulted the
victim with an intent to kill!

00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:17.325
[gasps]

00:10:17.408 --> 00:10:18.866
[JUDGE]
Hmm. That does make sense.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.575
[MIA]
Objection!

00:10:20.658 --> 00:10:21.950
[gasping]

00:10:22.033 --> 00:10:23.741
[PHOENIX]
Ms. Fey?

00:10:23.825 --> 00:10:25.950
Even if my client
did shove the victim,

00:10:26.033 --> 00:10:27.908
the blow did not
actually cause his death.

00:10:27.991 --> 00:10:29.116
This is not a murder!

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.450
Care to explain that, defense?

00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:33.158
Look at the autopsy report.

00:10:33.241 --> 00:10:36.033
It states the cause of
death was electrocution.

00:10:36.116 --> 00:10:37.783
He died by electrocution?

00:10:37.866 --> 00:10:39.241
Remember what
the weather was like?

00:10:39.325 --> 00:10:41.575
I mean it was raining cats
and dogs the entire day.

00:10:41.658 --> 00:10:43.700
[thunder cracks

00:10:43.783 --> 00:10:45.158
Considering that fact,

00:10:45.241 --> 00:10:47.283
it stands to reason the
most likely cause of death

00:10:47.366 --> 00:10:48.741
would be a lightning strike.

00:10:48.825 --> 00:10:50.158
[JUDGE]
It was an act of God?

00:10:50.241 --> 00:10:51.991
This wasn't a murder after all.

00:10:52.075 --> 00:10:54.491
But rather an unfortunate
freak accident!

00:10:54.575 --> 00:10:56.533
Oh, brilliant
deduction, Ms. Fey.

00:10:56.616 --> 00:10:59.408
[PAYNE chuckles] I wouldn't
begin the celebration yet

00:10:59.491 --> 00:11:01.158
if I were you, young rookie.

00:11:01.241 --> 00:11:03.325
A seasoned prosecutor
covers every base,

00:11:03.408 --> 00:11:06.408
so of course I investigated
the meteorological report.

00:11:06.491 --> 00:11:07.575
[MIA gasps]

00:11:07.658 --> 00:11:09.116
There were, in fact,
no lightning strikes

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.991
in that area on the
day of the murder.

00:11:11.075 --> 00:11:12.533
What? There weren't?

00:11:12.616 --> 00:11:14.783
Simply look at
the crime scene photo.

00:11:14.866 --> 00:11:18.158
And Mister Swallow's true cause
of death is clearly visible.

00:11:18.241 --> 00:11:19.908
[MIA]
That thing. Above him.

00:11:19.991 --> 00:11:22.033
Is that a severed
electric cable?

00:11:22.116 --> 00:11:24.658
Precisely. Your
client heartlessly pushed

00:11:24.741 --> 00:11:27.616
the victim toward that cable
hoping it would end his life.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.658
Which, as we all know,
was exactly the thing

00:11:29.741 --> 00:11:31.491
that killed Mister Swallow.

00:11:31.575 --> 00:11:33.325
[yelps]

00:11:33.408 --> 00:11:35.825
[MIA]
Was that all just a trap?

00:11:37.075 --> 00:11:39.533
The prosecution has
presented a credible motive

00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:41.741
and explained the method
of murder in this case.

00:11:41.825 --> 00:11:44.408
Hold on. No one's proven
Wright meant to kill him!

00:11:44.491 --> 00:11:46.491
Did he even know about
the severed cable?

00:11:46.575 --> 00:11:48.575
[coughs]

00:11:48.658 --> 00:11:51.950
It's so sad. The defense
has resorted to conjecture.

00:11:52.033 --> 00:11:54.033
Very well.
I suppose I'll spare you

00:11:54.116 --> 00:11:57.200
from any further desperation
and finish you off for good.

00:11:57.283 --> 00:11:58.450
What do you mean by that?

00:11:58.533 --> 00:12:00.200
[PAYNE]
The prosecution has a witness

00:12:00.283 --> 00:12:02.033
whose testimony is unassailable.

00:12:02.116 --> 00:12:04.283
[JUDGE] And who might
that be, Mister Payne?

00:12:04.366 --> 00:12:06.033
This witness has
had a horrifying image

00:12:06.116 --> 00:12:07.616
burned into their mind forever.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.658
They actually saw
the murder as it happened.

00:12:09.741 --> 00:12:10.658
[gasping]

00:12:10.741 --> 00:12:12.200
[JUDGE]
Did they now?

00:12:12.283 --> 00:12:15.325
[PAYNE chuckles] She has already
come up in this very trial.

00:12:15.408 --> 00:12:17.033
Her name is
Miss Dahlia Hawthorne!

00:12:17.116 --> 00:12:18.366
[MIA growls]

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:20.200
[PHOENIX] Oh, I knew
that my sweet little Dollie

00:12:20.283 --> 00:12:21.533
would come and save me!

00:12:21.616 --> 00:12:22.575
My love!

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:24.825
[coughs]

00:12:24.908 --> 00:12:26.366
[JUDGE]
Order in this court!

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:29.450
I call Miss Dahlia Hawthorne
to come to the witness stand!

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:36.825
[PHOENIX]
Dollie!

00:12:44.866 --> 00:12:46.825
[DAHLIA giggles]

00:12:46.908 --> 00:12:49.783
I'm afraid this witness
reeks of bad news for us.

00:12:49.866 --> 00:12:52.241
[MIA]
Hmph. I doubt that.

00:12:52.325 --> 00:12:55.575
In fact, this is just the
news I've been waiting for.

00:12:57.325 --> 00:13:00.450
Your time's up...
Dahlia Hawthorne!

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:03.783
[PAYNE]
If you would be so kind--

00:13:03.866 --> 00:13:05.991
Who are you, and what do you do?

00:13:06.075 --> 00:13:08.491
Who, me? Well, I, uh...

00:13:08.575 --> 00:13:09.950
Aww, poor thing.

00:13:10.033 --> 00:13:11.991
There's no reason for you
to be nervous, sweetie.

00:13:12.075 --> 00:13:14.033
Yeah! If anyone
even makes one rude remark

00:13:14.116 --> 00:13:16.075
toward you, I will make
them eat their words!

00:13:16.158 --> 00:13:18.825
I'll use my gavel to
teach them about respect!

00:13:18.908 --> 00:13:20.783
[MIA] How comforting
that they're glaring at me

00:13:20.866 --> 00:13:22.450
when they say that.

00:13:22.533 --> 00:13:24.241
You're both sweet.

00:13:24.325 --> 00:13:25.616
Oh, but of course.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.075
It's my pleasure, dear.

00:13:27.158 --> 00:13:29.700
I believe you'd asked for
her name and occupation?

00:13:29.783 --> 00:13:34.450
[DAHLIA] Hmm. You're still
the same as ever, Mia Fey.

00:13:34.533 --> 00:13:35.575
[MIA]
Hmph.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:41.116
Oh, my. Does this mean the two
of you are already acquainted?

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.866
We've met, just once.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.866
To answer your question,
my name is Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.950
A literature student
at Ivy University.

00:13:49.033 --> 00:13:51.033
It's truly an honor
to be here in the presence

00:13:51.116 --> 00:13:52.783
of such great legal minds.

00:13:52.866 --> 00:13:53.783
I'm honored, too.

00:13:53.866 --> 00:13:55.950
Yet still we try to stay humble.

00:13:56.033 --> 00:13:57.908
She wasted zero time
getting the old boys

00:13:57.991 --> 00:13:59.741
wrapped around her
little finger.

00:14:03.491 --> 00:14:05.616
[DAHLIA] That day, I
had gone over to meet

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.200
sweetie Feenie
after class let out.

00:14:08.283 --> 00:14:10.908
[JUDGE]
Who's that? Oh, the defendant?

00:14:10.991 --> 00:14:13.825
[DAHLIA] Yes, sir. I came
across Feenie and Dougie.

00:14:13.908 --> 00:14:15.616
They were having
some sort of conversation

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.116
behind the building.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.450
I was too far to hear
what they were saying,

00:14:20.533 --> 00:14:23.783
but all of a sudden Dougie got
angry and gave Feenie a big pow.

00:14:23.866 --> 00:14:26.241
Say what? The victim
pow'd the defendant?

00:14:26.325 --> 00:14:28.075
[DAHLIA] Yeah! I didn't see
Feenie do anything

00:14:28.158 --> 00:14:29.491
to deserve it!

00:14:29.575 --> 00:14:32.116
He had no choice but
to shove him back after that.

00:14:33.575 --> 00:14:35.450
[DAHLIA] Poor Dougie
slammed into the utility pole

00:14:35.533 --> 00:14:37.575
and snapped the electric cable.

00:14:39.825 --> 00:14:41.741
I could see Dougie
get up and desperately try

00:14:41.825 --> 00:14:44.950
to skedaddle his way outta
there, but Feeny followed him.

00:14:45.033 --> 00:14:47.408
He ran over and shoved him
again from the back,

00:14:47.491 --> 00:14:49.658
knocking him to the ground.

00:14:49.741 --> 00:14:51.741
And at the exact same
moment that Dougie collapsed,

00:14:51.825 --> 00:14:54.158
I heard an extremely loud,
cracking noise.

00:14:54.241 --> 00:14:56.075
I thought my little
heart was going to pitter-patter

00:14:56.158 --> 00:14:57.408
right out of my chest!

00:14:57.491 --> 00:15:00.075
I'm pitter-pattering
just hearing about it.

00:15:00.158 --> 00:15:02.075
A loud cracking noise, you say?

00:15:02.158 --> 00:15:03.950
There's no doubt that what
you heard must've been

00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:05.908
the victim being electrocuted.

00:15:05.991 --> 00:15:07.491
[DAHLIA] All of this happened
mere moments after

00:15:07.575 --> 00:15:09.991
that cable was knocked
loose and fell.

00:15:12.158 --> 00:15:13.241
[MIA gasps]

00:15:13.325 --> 00:15:15.866
Well then.
The witness's testimony

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.241
makes it crystal clear
how the murder happened.

00:15:18.325 --> 00:15:19.908
And the prosecution
has also gathered

00:15:19.991 --> 00:15:21.783
corroborating testimony.

00:15:21.866 --> 00:15:23.408
Oh? Who'd you get that from?

00:15:23.491 --> 00:15:25.741
[PAYNE] The science majors
who were conducting experiments

00:15:25.825 --> 00:15:27.533
in one of the labs nearby.

00:15:27.616 --> 00:15:29.825
Allow me to read
their prepared statement.

00:15:29.908 --> 00:15:32.491
"Around 3 PM, all of the
electrical equipment in the lab

00:15:32.575 --> 00:15:34.741
simultaneously lost power."

00:15:34.825 --> 00:15:37.408
[JUDGE]
So, was there a blackout?

00:15:37.491 --> 00:15:39.450
[PAYNE] Yes. There are
logs of a blackout taking

00:15:39.533 --> 00:15:41.616
place at 2:55 PM.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:43.283
The equipment
in that particular lab

00:15:43.366 --> 00:15:45.325
requires high
voltage to operate.

00:15:45.408 --> 00:15:47.325
Which was being supplied
by the cable that had been

00:15:47.408 --> 00:15:49.700
severed at that time.

00:15:49.783 --> 00:15:53.158
The defendant met with the
victim at 2:45 that afternoon.

00:15:53.241 --> 00:15:55.825
And a mere ten minutes later he
had caused the untimely death

00:15:55.908 --> 00:15:57.616
of poor Mister Swallow.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.241
This is the shocking
truth of what happened

00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:00.825
that fateful day!

00:16:00.908 --> 00:16:02.783
[CROWD murmurin]

00:16:02.866 --> 00:16:06.033
[JUDGE] Hmm. There's
little room for doubt.

00:16:06.116 --> 00:16:08.616
Thanks for your brave
and helpful testimony.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:09.950
Thank you.

00:16:10.033 --> 00:16:11.616
I couldn't hide the truth
from you, Your Honor.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.575
[MIA]
Objection!

00:16:12.658 --> 00:16:14.450
--[yells]
--[screams]

00:16:16.075 --> 00:16:18.825
I hate to break it to you,
but that's not going to fly.

00:16:18.908 --> 00:16:20.200
Huh?

00:16:20.283 --> 00:16:21.658
[MIA] The only thing brave
about her testimony...

00:16:21.741 --> 00:16:23.575
...is that she's
risking perjury!

00:16:23.658 --> 00:16:25.616
[PAYNE]
Really? In what way?

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:26.741
[DAHLIA growls]

00:16:26.825 --> 00:16:29.325
The electric cable
was severed at 2:55.

00:16:29.408 --> 00:16:32.783
This must be when my client
admittedly shoved the victim.

00:16:32.866 --> 00:16:34.741
But looking at
the crime scene photo.

00:16:34.825 --> 00:16:38.241
We can see the victim's watch
stopped functioning at 3:05.

00:16:38.325 --> 00:16:40.158
How can you explain
the ten minute gap?

00:16:40.241 --> 00:16:41.450
[gasping]

00:16:41.533 --> 00:16:42.658
[gasps]

00:16:42.741 --> 00:16:44.783
In the sworn testimony
you gave the court,

00:16:44.866 --> 00:16:46.991
you stated that the incident
took place mere moments

00:16:47.075 --> 00:16:48.991
after the cable was
severed right?

00:16:49.075 --> 00:16:51.200
I'll ask again!

00:16:51.283 --> 00:16:53.283
Do you have any
reasonable explanation

00:16:53.366 --> 00:16:54.491
for this discrepancy?

00:16:54.575 --> 00:16:55.408
[DAHLIA whimpers]

00:16:55.491 --> 00:16:56.741
[yelps]

00:16:56.825 --> 00:17:00.491
[CROWD murmurin]

00:17:00.575 --> 00:17:02.158
Tell me, Miss Hawthorne.

00:17:02.241 --> 00:17:04.658
Why must you continuously
spout these lies?

00:17:04.741 --> 00:17:05.908
What?

00:17:05.991 --> 00:17:06.866
[MIA] It's almost like
you're actively trying

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.491
to frame your boyfriend.

00:17:08.575 --> 00:17:09.408
[DAHLIA growls]

00:17:09.491 --> 00:17:10.866
--[JUDGE] Hmm?
--[PAYNE gasps]

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:13.408
[PHOENIX] But... why would
she wanna frame me?

00:17:13.491 --> 00:17:19.450
[CROWD murmuring]

00:17:19.533 --> 00:17:22.616
[MIA] You seem to be a magnet
for tragic incidents like this.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:25.241
The last one was
only eight months ago.

00:17:25.325 --> 00:17:27.616
[JUDGE]
Hmm? What happened then?

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:29.491
[DAHLIA gasps, growls]

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.700
To jog your memory,
this particular event took place

00:17:34.783 --> 00:17:36.658
in this courthouse.

00:17:36.741 --> 00:17:37.783
Observe.

00:17:37.866 --> 00:17:39.325
[PAYNE]
What is it?

00:17:39.408 --> 00:17:43.491
[JUDGE] Hm. I remember now.
What a shock that was.

00:17:43.575 --> 00:17:45.866
[MIA] Miss Hawthorne.
You were on the scene as well,

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.866
when that terrible
incident took place.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.200
[DAHLIA gasps]

00:17:49.283 --> 00:17:50.408
[MIA] When researching
the investigation reports

00:17:50.491 --> 00:17:52.325
submitted at the time,

00:17:52.408 --> 00:17:55.533
I couldn't help but notice
who was the prime suspect.

00:17:55.616 --> 00:17:56.991
It was you!

00:17:57.075 --> 00:17:58.950
That's totally ludicrous!

00:17:59.033 --> 00:18:01.200
[PHOENIX]
Dollie was the prime suspect?

00:18:01.283 --> 00:18:02.658
I don't believe it.

00:18:02.741 --> 00:18:05.200
The crime that rocked this
courthouse eight months ago

00:18:05.283 --> 00:18:06.866
has a link to this case.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.366
--Say wha...?
--And what would that be,

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.575
--defense?
--There was a trial going on.

00:18:10.658 --> 00:18:11.991
The defense lawyer
summoned a witness

00:18:12.075 --> 00:18:13.325
to come in for questioning.

00:18:13.408 --> 00:18:16.033
And they are the link
to this current case.

00:18:16.116 --> 00:18:19.241
The witness
was Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:18:19.325 --> 00:18:20.616
[DAHLIA growls]

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.575
[MIA] She met the lawyer
in the cafeteria downstairs.

00:18:26.616 --> 00:18:28.241
[MIA] And that's where
it all happened.

00:18:30.491 --> 00:18:32.116
Somebody laced
the coffee that lawyer

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:34.741
was drinking with poison.
And Miss Hawthorne was named

00:18:34.825 --> 00:18:36.741
suspect number
one in that crime.

00:18:36.825 --> 00:18:38.491
[PHOENIX]
Not my sweet Dollie.

00:18:38.575 --> 00:18:40.116
No. It's not true.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.533
I have a request.

00:18:41.616 --> 00:18:44.158
No, a demand, that Miss
Hawthorne give sworn testimony

00:18:44.241 --> 00:18:46.033
regarding that incident
before this court!

00:18:46.116 --> 00:18:47.325
[PAYNE]
Objection!

00:18:47.408 --> 00:18:49.700
What? That's completely absurd!

00:18:49.783 --> 00:18:51.033
I won't stand for this!

00:18:51.116 --> 00:18:52.158
I, uh...

00:18:52.241 --> 00:18:53.616
I fail to see how
an isolated incident

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.741
has anything to
do with this case!

00:18:54.825 --> 00:18:56.325
[DAHLIA]
Mister Prosecutor?

00:18:56.408 --> 00:18:59.200
I believe I was speaking,
when you interrupted me.

00:18:59.283 --> 00:19:03.741
Oh. I'm sorry. Go ahead, dear.

00:19:03.825 --> 00:19:05.116
I appreciate it.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:07.241
And what Ms. Fey
was saying is true.

00:19:07.325 --> 00:19:09.991
Eight months ago, I was
under a suspicious eyeball.

00:19:10.075 --> 00:19:12.658
[JUDGE] You mean...
The police were eyeballing you?

00:19:12.741 --> 00:19:15.783
[DAHLIA] That's why I wanna set
the record straight for good.

00:19:15.866 --> 00:19:19.408
And prove beyond any doubt
I had absolutely no part in it!

00:19:19.491 --> 00:19:20.700
But... There's no need

00:19:20.783 --> 00:19:22.200
for you to go through
all that trauma again!

00:19:22.283 --> 00:19:23.825
[gavel bangs]

00:19:23.908 --> 00:19:25.700
The end goal
of this trial today,

00:19:25.783 --> 00:19:28.450
is to figure out who's at
fault for a loss of life.

00:19:28.533 --> 00:19:30.408
You believe her
testimony on that case

00:19:30.491 --> 00:19:31.950
will help us reach that goal?

00:19:32.033 --> 00:19:33.533
I do.

00:19:33.616 --> 00:19:36.616
Then the prosecution's
objection is overruled.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:39.033
I appreciate it, Your Honor.

00:19:39.116 --> 00:19:40.116
[PHOENIX]
Dollie...

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.950
[PAYNE whines]

00:19:42.033 --> 00:19:44.283
[MIA] All right, now that I've
tied the two crimes together,

00:19:44.366 --> 00:19:47.116
I need to stay on the offensive.
I've got this!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.700
Excellent move, Ms. Fey.

00:19:48.783 --> 00:19:51.200
I finally understand why you
were so hell-bent on taking on

00:19:51.283 --> 00:19:52.533
this particular case.

00:19:52.616 --> 00:19:53.908
I had my reasons.

00:19:53.991 --> 00:19:57.491
Oh. This kind of spunk
lights a fire inside me!

00:19:57.575 --> 00:20:00.241
Go on and take no prisoners!
Give 'em hell!

00:20:00.325 --> 00:20:01.741
Right!

00:20:01.825 --> 00:20:03.450
Things are about to get real!

00:20:03.533 --> 00:20:06.200
I'll make you proud.
Just watch me!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.241
Now, Miss Hawthorne,

00:20:10.325 --> 00:20:12.283
you know what's expected of you.

00:20:12.366 --> 00:20:15.658
Tell us about the events
of eight months ago.

00:20:15.741 --> 00:20:17.741
That day, I was
meeting with the lawyer

00:20:17.825 --> 00:20:20.783
in the cafeteria downstairs
to discuss something.

00:20:20.866 --> 00:20:23.200
I left my seat briefly,
just for a moment,

00:20:23.283 --> 00:20:25.575
and that's when it happened.

00:20:25.658 --> 00:20:26.991
When I came back to the table.

00:20:27.075 --> 00:20:30.325
I found him lying prone
on the floor.

00:20:30.408 --> 00:20:33.241
You say you left your
seat for "just a moment."

00:20:33.325 --> 00:20:35.533
How long was it, exactly?

00:20:35.616 --> 00:20:37.950
If I were to
guess at a specific time?

00:20:38.033 --> 00:20:39.575
Ten to 20 minutes.

00:20:39.658 --> 00:20:41.450
[MIA] Why did you leave
and where did you go?

00:20:41.533 --> 00:20:44.241
[gasps]
Well, I, uh...

00:20:44.325 --> 00:20:48.116
Huh. There are some things a
lady doesn't need to divulge.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:50.700
Anyway, the police
investigated her back then,

00:20:50.783 --> 00:20:53.533
so this line of
questioning is redundant.

00:20:53.616 --> 00:20:54.866
I concur.

00:20:56.533 --> 00:20:58.866
[DAHLIA]
According to the constabulary,

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:02.366
they discovered some traces of
a lethal poison in the coffee.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:04.616
Supposedly,
a special kind of poison.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.908
What does that mean?

00:21:05.991 --> 00:21:07.616
[DAHLIA]
Well. They said it was purified

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.325
through a very unique
chemical process.

00:21:10.408 --> 00:21:11.866
I'd like to point
out this young lady

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.575
studies literature,
not advanced chemistry.

00:21:14.658 --> 00:21:17.491
Right. Anyway,
once the authorities arrived.

00:21:17.575 --> 00:21:19.283
I was thoroughly
frisked for evidence.

00:21:19.366 --> 00:21:21.200
What? No way!

00:21:21.283 --> 00:21:23.033
Those swine! How dare they?

00:21:23.116 --> 00:21:24.658
[coughs]

00:21:24.741 --> 00:21:27.533
Obviously, they
didn't find any poison on me.

00:21:27.616 --> 00:21:30.325
Nothing. So that
proves my innocence!

00:21:30.408 --> 00:21:31.700
She's right!

00:21:31.783 --> 00:21:33.366
My Dollie is the most
innocent girl I've ever met!

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:34.950
About this poison.

00:21:35.033 --> 00:21:37.700
Do you happen to know how
large a dose he was given?

00:21:37.783 --> 00:21:40.908
I don't.
Sorry, they didn't tell me.

00:21:40.991 --> 00:21:42.741
Oh. Ms. Fey.

00:21:42.825 --> 00:21:46.491
According to the officer I spoke
with, it was a liquid poison.

00:21:46.575 --> 00:21:49.783
Small enough to be contained
inside an eyedropper bottle.

00:21:49.866 --> 00:21:51.325
That's not very much at all.

00:21:51.408 --> 00:21:52.866
[JUDGE]
After the incident,

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.033
the entire courthouse was turned
upside down in the search.

00:21:56.116 --> 00:21:57.991
But unfortunately,
there was no small vessel

00:21:58.075 --> 00:22:00.158
like that to be found
anywhere in the building.

00:22:00.241 --> 00:22:01.908
[PAYNE]
So, no trace of it?

00:22:01.991 --> 00:22:03.116
[CROWD gasping]

00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:04.700
[MIA]
By the way. If you would...

00:22:04.783 --> 00:22:06.491
Can you tell us what
you were here to discuss

00:22:06.575 --> 00:22:08.158
with the lawyer that day?

00:22:10.366 --> 00:22:13.075
It was in regard to an
incident that I was swept up in

00:22:13.158 --> 00:22:15.200
when I was just a little girl.

00:22:15.283 --> 00:22:19.033
For some reason he
wanted to talk to me about it.

00:22:19.116 --> 00:22:21.241
Will you share with the
court what that incident was?

00:22:21.325 --> 00:22:22.658
Objection!

00:22:22.741 --> 00:22:24.616
Whatever it is, I'm sure it has
absolutely nothing to do

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:25.908
with this trial, Your Honor!

00:22:25.991 --> 00:22:27.575
Objection sustained.

00:22:27.658 --> 00:22:29.700
The defense's question
will hereby be stricken

00:22:29.783 --> 00:22:31.450
from the record.

00:22:33.325 --> 00:22:35.075
[MIA] You seem to get
"swept up," as you say,

00:22:35.158 --> 00:22:37.991
in a fair number of
incidents, right?

00:22:38.075 --> 00:22:40.908
When you were younger,
eight months ago,

00:22:40.991 --> 00:22:42.783
and now, this one.

00:22:42.866 --> 00:22:44.658
Looking at the
specifics of that case,

00:22:44.741 --> 00:22:47.658
the tragedy with the lawyer
occurred on the 27th of August

00:22:47.741 --> 00:22:49.033
this past year.

00:22:49.116 --> 00:22:51.908
You certainly have
had an abundance of misfortune.

00:22:51.991 --> 00:22:53.450
Yes, that's true.

00:22:53.533 --> 00:22:56.491
Sometimes, I feel like I must've
been born under a bad sign.

00:22:56.575 --> 00:22:57.616
[PHOENIX wails]

00:22:57.700 --> 00:22:59.908
Oh. My. What's wrong with you?

00:22:59.991 --> 00:23:04.283
August 27th?
That was our day of destiny!

00:23:04.366 --> 00:23:05.491
Meaning what exactly?

00:23:05.575 --> 00:23:07.116
That was the day
Dollie and I first embarked

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:10.325
upon our love journey together,
inside this courthouse!

00:23:10.408 --> 00:23:11.325
[JUDGE gasping]

00:23:11.408 --> 00:23:12.325
[DAHLIA growls]

00:23:12.408 --> 00:23:13.950
You remember
that magical moment!

00:23:14.033 --> 00:23:15.366
Right, babe?

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:16.991
When we first met down in
the basement reading room?

00:23:17.075 --> 00:23:20.491
Feenie. Not now.
That's between us.

00:23:20.575 --> 00:23:22.075
You met Miss
Hawthorne down there?

00:23:22.158 --> 00:23:23.658
You bet!

00:23:23.741 --> 00:23:25.991
I was studying in the reading
room when my angel descended.

00:23:26.075 --> 00:23:29.283
My soul mate was sent to me
straight from Heaven!

00:23:29.366 --> 00:23:30.908
The moment we
laid eyes on each other,

00:23:30.991 --> 00:23:33.200
the air itself became electric!

00:23:33.283 --> 00:23:35.866
We're living proof
of love at first sight!

00:23:37.033 --> 00:23:38.783
And she is so generous!

00:23:38.866 --> 00:23:41.075
She gave me this
pendant right then!

00:23:41.158 --> 00:23:43.908
A symbol of our undying love!

00:23:43.991 --> 00:23:45.575
She took one
look at me and said,

00:23:45.658 --> 00:23:47.283
"I want you to have this."

00:23:47.366 --> 00:23:50.741
And she shyly took it off
her neck and put it on mine!

00:23:50.825 --> 00:23:54.366
Oh, wow. So she gave
this to you that very day?

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:56.075
--Just on a whim?
--She did!

00:23:56.158 --> 00:23:59.325
It fills me with so much joy,
I show it to everyone I meet.

00:23:59.408 --> 00:24:01.366
Joy is contagious,
and I'm trying to spread

00:24:01.450 --> 00:24:02.616
--as much as I can.
--[DAHLIA] Feenie, I said...

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:04.783
But she gets
embarrassed so darn easily.

00:24:04.866 --> 00:24:06.825
So every time that
we've met up lately,

00:24:06.908 --> 00:24:09.200
she tries to make me
give it back to her.

00:24:09.283 --> 00:24:11.950
Give it back?
But it was a gift, right?

00:24:12.033 --> 00:24:14.116
Huh. Seems odd to me.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:17.075
Ha! Well, she's definitely
a one-in-a-million girl!

00:24:17.158 --> 00:24:19.491
Even on the day I met Doug,
she was like, "Give it back!"

00:24:19.575 --> 00:24:21.200
and I was like, "But I'm
so proud of our love!"

00:24:21.283 --> 00:24:22.491
Feenie, stop!

00:24:22.575 --> 00:24:23.408
[gasps]

00:24:23.491 --> 00:24:25.991
[DAHLIA growls]

00:24:26.075 --> 00:24:28.366
Enough! I will have order!

00:24:29.950 --> 00:24:33.033
Ah! [coughs]

00:24:33.116 --> 00:24:36.783
Let go! [coughs]

00:24:36.866 --> 00:24:38.033
[gasps]

00:24:40.741 --> 00:24:41.908
[MIA]
Eight months ago,

00:24:41.991 --> 00:24:44.033
Dahlia Hawthorne left
her seat at the table,

00:24:44.116 --> 00:24:46.366
and my colleague
collapsed onto the floor.

00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:49.325
That same day, she met
Mister Wright in this building,

00:24:49.408 --> 00:24:51.033
and gave him a strange pendant.

00:24:52.825 --> 00:24:54.783
It's perfectly clear to me now.

00:24:54.866 --> 00:24:57.658
[JUDGE]
Hmm? Well, that makes one of us.

00:24:57.741 --> 00:24:58.825
Your Honor,

00:24:58.908 --> 00:25:01.325
I know what happened
eight months ago.

00:25:01.408 --> 00:25:04.991
And the one who
poisoned that cup of coffee...

00:25:05.075 --> 00:25:07.616
...was this woman,
Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:25:07.700 --> 00:25:09.533
No, that's impossible.

00:25:09.616 --> 00:25:12.741
Remember? The police patted
me down and searched me.

00:25:12.825 --> 00:25:15.575
Of course, they didn't
find any trace of poison.

00:25:15.658 --> 00:25:17.158
What's more...

00:25:17.241 --> 00:25:18.991
The poison container was nowhere
to be found in the courthouse.

00:25:19.075 --> 00:25:21.866
You have no evidence
to support this claim!

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:24.908
Because all you had
to do was hide the container.

00:25:24.991 --> 00:25:26.741
Somewhere they
wouldn't think to look for it.

00:25:26.825 --> 00:25:27.825
[DAHLIA growls]

00:25:27.908 --> 00:25:29.325
[PAYNE]
But they searched everywhere!

00:25:29.408 --> 00:25:32.075
Right? Every corner.
High and low.

00:25:32.158 --> 00:25:35.241
Tell us. Just where
did she hide it?

00:25:35.325 --> 00:25:37.075
[MIA]
This is a pivotal moment.

00:25:37.158 --> 00:25:39.450
I've reached the
point of no return.

00:25:39.533 --> 00:25:42.866
That day, after you had
poisoned the lawyer's coffee,

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:46.241
you left your seat, so you could
go and dispose of the evidence.

00:25:46.325 --> 00:25:48.825
Immediately afterward,
by some miracle of fate,

00:25:48.908 --> 00:25:50.491
in the basement
of this courthouse,

00:25:50.575 --> 00:25:52.158
you met your new boyfriend.

00:25:52.241 --> 00:25:53.075
[gasps]

00:25:53.158 --> 00:25:55.200
Uh, what? Hang on.

00:25:55.283 --> 00:25:56.450
[MIA]
But in truth...

00:25:56.533 --> 00:25:58.241
What she'd really found
on that eventful day,

00:25:58.325 --> 00:26:00.200
was the perfect hiding place.

00:26:00.283 --> 00:26:02.158
Somebody completely unrelated.

00:26:02.241 --> 00:26:04.533
A person the cops
would never think to search.

00:26:04.616 --> 00:26:05.575
A rube.

00:26:07.075 --> 00:26:09.200
That man is right there.

00:26:09.283 --> 00:26:10.241
Phoenix Wright.

00:26:10.325 --> 00:26:12.741
[PHOENIX]
Uhh...

00:26:12.825 --> 00:26:15.158
What? No... Don't tell me!

00:26:15.241 --> 00:26:17.866
Hidden in the pendant?

00:26:17.950 --> 00:26:19.700
There is a very
high likelihood it contains

00:26:19.783 --> 00:26:21.616
the same deadly poison.

00:26:21.700 --> 00:26:24.866
[CROWD gasping, murmuring]

00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:26.825
If you look at it closely,

00:26:26.908 --> 00:26:30.033
you can see there is still some
liquid remaining in the bottle.

00:26:30.116 --> 00:26:31.950
It must be analyzed at once!

00:26:32.033 --> 00:26:33.241
[screams]

00:26:33.325 --> 00:26:34.241
[CROWD murmuring]

00:26:34.325 --> 00:26:35.825
[JUDGE]
Order! Order, please!

00:26:35.908 --> 00:26:37.241
Calm yourselves!

00:26:37.325 --> 00:26:39.950
Now, what's going on here?

00:26:40.033 --> 00:26:41.200
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:26:41.283 --> 00:26:43.908
On behalf of
sweet Dollie, I object!

00:26:43.991 --> 00:26:45.741
Wait! Seriously?

00:26:45.825 --> 00:26:48.200
[JUDGE] I warned you,
defendant! Get back!

00:26:48.283 --> 00:26:51.450
Ah! No! It's not right!

00:26:51.533 --> 00:26:54.200
My girlfriend would never
do anything like that!

00:26:54.283 --> 00:26:55.783
But how can you be so sure?

00:26:55.866 --> 00:26:58.158
First off... Because...

00:26:58.241 --> 00:26:59.991
I mean, there's no way
she could've whipped up

00:27:00.075 --> 00:27:01.408
some kind of specialized poison.

00:27:01.491 --> 00:27:02.991
Yeah! Right!

00:27:03.075 --> 00:27:06.241
It took knowledge of advanced
chemical processes to purify it!

00:27:06.325 --> 00:27:07.700
Dollie's an artist.

00:27:07.783 --> 00:27:10.200
She would have no idea
how to go about that!

00:27:10.283 --> 00:27:14.116
Sorry. All she had to do
was know where to find it.

00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:15.575
[gasps]

00:27:15.658 --> 00:27:19.366
[MIA] Just think. What was
the victim's field of study?

00:27:19.450 --> 00:27:21.950
It was pharmacology, remember?

00:27:22.033 --> 00:27:24.283
If she could access his lab,

00:27:24.366 --> 00:27:27.658
she could then procure all
manner of poisonous chemicals.

00:27:27.741 --> 00:27:29.075
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:27:32.116 --> 00:27:33.658
Mister Wright,
I ask that you please

00:27:33.741 --> 00:27:35.908
hand over that pendant.

00:27:35.991 --> 00:27:38.033
If we can analyze it,
you could leave this courtroom

00:27:38.116 --> 00:27:39.200
as a free man.

00:27:39.283 --> 00:27:40.408
[PHOENIX groans]

00:27:40.491 --> 00:27:42.783
What do you say?

00:27:42.866 --> 00:27:44.450
[PHOENIX]
What do you think?

00:27:44.533 --> 00:27:46.366
I say...

00:27:46.450 --> 00:27:48.908
There's no freaking way!

00:27:48.991 --> 00:27:49.908
[wails, sobs]

00:27:49.991 --> 00:27:51.283
[PAYNE]
Where could he be going?!

00:27:51.366 --> 00:27:54.116
[JUDGE] Bailiffs! Don't
let him leave the building!

00:27:54.200 --> 00:27:55.533
The boy's gone nuts.

00:27:55.616 --> 00:27:57.158
Is he pleading insanity?

00:27:59.950 --> 00:28:01.491
What is he thinking?

00:28:06.116 --> 00:28:08.575
What kind of fool
tries to flee a courtroom?

00:28:08.658 --> 00:28:10.158
Have you no sense, boy?

00:28:10.241 --> 00:28:12.200
[PHOENIX]
I'm sorry, sir...

00:28:12.283 --> 00:28:13.283
[banging]

00:28:13.366 --> 00:28:14.866
[PAYNE]
If apologies worked in court,

00:28:14.950 --> 00:28:16.533
all of us would be out of a job!

00:28:16.616 --> 00:28:17.991
Anyway.

00:28:18.075 --> 00:28:21.075
Mister Wright, will you please
hand over the pendant?

00:28:21.158 --> 00:28:23.450
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:28:23.533 --> 00:28:25.491
[MIA]
You do have it, correct?

00:28:25.575 --> 00:28:28.825
[PHOENIX sighs]
I'm sorry!

00:28:28.908 --> 00:28:32.366
Uh... [gasps] Sorry for what?

00:28:32.450 --> 00:28:36.366
[PHOENIX sighs]
For... eating it.

00:28:37.575 --> 00:28:39.200
[BOTH sigh]

00:28:40.283 --> 00:28:42.200
--Huh?
--[MIA] What did he say?!

00:28:42.283 --> 00:28:43.825
[PHOENIX]
Yeah. It was too big.

00:28:43.908 --> 00:28:46.950
So I had to break it into
little pieces and chew it.

00:28:47.033 --> 00:28:48.116
[groans]

00:28:48.200 --> 00:28:51.033
You... did... what...?

00:28:51.116 --> 00:28:52.491
[wails]

00:28:52.575 --> 00:28:54.866
[screams]

00:28:54.950 --> 00:28:56.158
[PHOENIX sobs]

00:28:56.241 --> 00:28:58.075
Mr. Wright! Are you okay?!

00:28:58.158 --> 00:29:00.575
That botttle--
There was poison in it!

00:29:00.658 --> 00:29:03.533
[DAHLIA cackles] I bet
you're really disappointed

00:29:03.616 --> 00:29:06.158
that he didn't die, huh?

00:29:06.241 --> 00:29:07.575
Aren't you, hag?

00:29:07.658 --> 00:29:08.783
[MIA gasps]

00:29:08.866 --> 00:29:10.950
Because...
the fact he's alive

00:29:11.033 --> 00:29:12.950
proves there wasn't
any poison in there.

00:29:13.033 --> 00:29:15.075
[MIA] But that tiny little bit
that was left probably

00:29:15.158 --> 00:29:16.783
wasn't enough to do anything.

00:29:16.866 --> 00:29:17.950
And besides...

00:29:19.366 --> 00:29:20.950
It has been eight months!

00:29:21.033 --> 00:29:22.908
Maybe it lost its potency!

00:29:22.991 --> 00:29:24.075
Think so?

00:29:24.158 --> 00:29:25.658
[MIA gulps]

00:29:25.741 --> 00:29:27.575
[DAHLIA chuckles] Talking down
to me without proof I've done

00:29:27.658 --> 00:29:30.325
anything wrong must
be an old lady thing.

00:29:30.408 --> 00:29:32.741
Yeah. Wouldn't
you agree, grandpa?

00:29:32.825 --> 00:29:35.616
Huh? Uh... I guess.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:36.908
In any case...

00:29:38.741 --> 00:29:41.116
Right now, the victim is dead.

00:29:41.200 --> 00:29:43.783
The pendant is inside
the defendant's belly.

00:29:43.866 --> 00:29:46.991
You don't have any decisive
evidence against Miss Hawthorne.

00:29:47.075 --> 00:29:48.241
Or do you, defense?

00:29:48.325 --> 00:29:49.325
[MIA growls]

00:29:49.408 --> 00:29:51.450
You're here
to defend your client.

00:29:51.533 --> 00:29:53.575
Trusting him is
the noble thing to do.

00:29:53.658 --> 00:29:55.325
It's actually rather
heartwarming to see

00:29:55.408 --> 00:29:56.991
how much faith
you've put in the boy.

00:29:57.075 --> 00:29:58.200
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:29:58.283 --> 00:30:01.658
[PAYNE] But! The prosecution
is no different!

00:30:01.741 --> 00:30:04.616
I would trust my very
life on Miss Hawthorne's word!

00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:07.075
I take her testimony
as absolute truth!

00:30:07.158 --> 00:30:08.991
Which is why I state
without fear of reproach

00:30:09.075 --> 00:30:11.783
that your deduction
was pure fantasy.

00:30:11.866 --> 00:30:13.241
Well. I'm done.

00:30:13.325 --> 00:30:15.116
What a total waste of my time.

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:17.908
Can someone remind me who
started this whole witch hunt,

00:30:17.991 --> 00:30:21.991
and tried to drag a completely
unrelated case into this one?

00:30:22.075 --> 00:30:23.950
I was under the
impression we were here today

00:30:24.033 --> 00:30:25.533
to solve Dougie's murder.

00:30:25.616 --> 00:30:28.700
Am I wrong? Old hag.

00:30:28.783 --> 00:30:30.866
[PHOENIX]
Whoa. Dollie...?

00:30:30.950 --> 00:30:32.366
[MIA]
I've almost got her.

00:30:32.450 --> 00:30:34.158
I can't let her just
stroll out of here,

00:30:34.241 --> 00:30:36.825
but I have to find the
evidence to nail her.

00:30:36.908 --> 00:30:39.533
It seems you've
reached a dead end.

00:30:39.616 --> 00:30:42.533
[MIA growls]
Please, Mister Wright!

00:30:42.616 --> 00:30:45.450
The truth. You need
to start telling the truth!

00:30:45.533 --> 00:30:48.408
Not the lies she fed you!
I know you're better than this.

00:30:48.491 --> 00:30:50.533
You can be a voice for justice!

00:30:50.616 --> 00:30:52.575
[PHOENIX]
I... don't know.

00:30:52.658 --> 00:30:54.825
The time has come for you
to start doing what's right,

00:30:54.908 --> 00:30:57.866
Mister Wright! We can't find
the truth without your help!

00:30:57.950 --> 00:31:02.700
[PHOENIX]
Me? Really? You need my help?

00:31:02.783 --> 00:31:04.200
Very well.

00:31:04.283 --> 00:31:06.450
Now that the cloud of suspicion
surrounding Miss Hawthorne

00:31:06.533 --> 00:31:08.741
has been cleared up, the line
of questioning regarding

00:31:08.825 --> 00:31:10.283
old cases will come to an en--

00:31:10.366 --> 00:31:11.366
Hold it, judge!

00:31:11.450 --> 00:31:13.283
[gasping

00:31:13.366 --> 00:31:15.075
[PHOENIX]
I'm so sorry, Ms. Fey.

00:31:15.158 --> 00:31:17.200
You believed in me and
were willing to stake

00:31:17.283 --> 00:31:20.616
your reputation on my word.
I've let you down...

00:31:20.700 --> 00:31:21.908
Mister Wright...

00:31:23.825 --> 00:31:25.616
[PHOENIX]
But I can't keep this up.

00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:27.866
I need to tell you
what really happened.

00:31:27.950 --> 00:31:29.033
It's not what you said?

00:31:29.116 --> 00:31:30.658
Feenie. Careful.

00:31:30.741 --> 00:31:34.325
[PHOENIX]
Mm-mm. Sorry, Dollie.

00:31:34.408 --> 00:31:37.616
I'm done lying.
I can't keep covering for you.

00:31:37.700 --> 00:31:39.533
Ugh! Feenie!

00:31:39.616 --> 00:31:43.116
Your time is up!
It's his turn to testify!

00:31:43.200 --> 00:31:44.200
[DAHLIA growls]

00:31:44.283 --> 00:31:45.533
I'll tell you
everything I know

00:31:45.616 --> 00:31:47.450
about what happened that day.

00:31:47.533 --> 00:31:50.158
The day Doug Swallow
was murdered.

00:31:50.241 --> 00:31:52.408
[DOUG] Listen, man.
You should stop seeing her.

00:31:52.491 --> 00:31:53.783
[PHOENIX] What?
How is our relationship

00:31:53.866 --> 00:31:55.366
any of your business?

00:31:55.450 --> 00:31:57.283
Please, this is
for your own sake.

00:31:57.366 --> 00:31:59.491
She's bad news, and
that's putting it lightly.

00:31:59.575 --> 00:32:01.200
[PHOENIX growls]
You're lying!

00:32:01.283 --> 00:32:02.741
[DOUG] There's something you
need to know about her.

00:32:02.825 --> 00:32:05.283
Before you get hurt.

00:32:05.366 --> 00:32:07.241
She stole poison
from our lab and I'm scared

00:32:07.325 --> 00:32:08.283
of what she'll do with it.

00:32:08.366 --> 00:32:09.991
No. Seriously?

00:32:10.075 --> 00:32:12.658
[DOUG] Mm-hmm.
Look, she's done it before.

00:32:12.741 --> 00:32:15.325
Eight months ago,
a drug sample came up missing.

00:32:15.408 --> 00:32:18.200
We noticed it immediately
after she dropped by the lab.

00:32:18.283 --> 00:32:20.075
I know it was her.
Without a doubt!

00:32:20.158 --> 00:32:21.325
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:32:22.116 --> 00:32:23.200
Shut your mouth!

00:32:23.283 --> 00:32:25.575
She's not like that!
There's no way!

00:32:25.658 --> 00:32:26.825
[DOUG grunts]

00:32:30.325 --> 00:32:31.616
[PAYNE]
Bah. What rubbish!

00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:33.991
[MIA] Did Mister Swallow
really tell you all of that?

00:32:34.075 --> 00:32:37.075
[DAHLIA] You're full of it!
That's a lie and you know it!

00:32:37.158 --> 00:32:38.491
[PHOENIX]
After I pushed him,

00:32:38.575 --> 00:32:41.075
I got out of there as fast
as I possibly could.

00:32:41.158 --> 00:32:44.033
But I got worried, so I came
back a little bit later.

00:32:45.950 --> 00:32:47.741
And I saw Dollie
kneeling over him.

00:32:47.825 --> 00:32:49.783
[CROWD gasping]

00:32:49.866 --> 00:32:50.950
[DAHLIA growls]

00:32:52.533 --> 00:32:53.575
[DAHLIA gasps]

00:32:55.658 --> 00:32:57.408
[gasps]

00:32:57.491 --> 00:32:58.741
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:33:04.575 --> 00:33:08.283
But she told me
that I had to swear on my life

00:33:08.366 --> 00:33:09.783
that I wouldn't tell anybody.

00:33:11.741 --> 00:33:13.241
I'm so sorry!

00:33:13.325 --> 00:33:16.533
[MIA] I knew it. She stole
that poison eight months ago.

00:33:16.616 --> 00:33:18.533
And now she's done it again.

00:33:18.616 --> 00:33:20.033
I can win this.

00:33:20.116 --> 00:33:22.491
With his testimony,
I can finally make the link

00:33:22.575 --> 00:33:24.783
between the two cases.

00:33:24.866 --> 00:33:26.658
[MIA] The night before Doug
Swallow's young life

00:33:26.741 --> 00:33:28.283
was tragically cut short,

00:33:28.366 --> 00:33:31.325
Dahlia Hawthorne stole
poison from his lab.

00:33:31.408 --> 00:33:32.783
Her motive was simple.

00:33:34.616 --> 00:33:36.116
She committed the
theft because murder

00:33:36.200 --> 00:33:37.575
was next on her agenda.

00:33:37.658 --> 00:33:39.033
To poison someone?

00:33:39.116 --> 00:33:40.991
What? That's ridiculous!

00:33:41.075 --> 00:33:43.491
Doug Swallow's cause of
death was electrocution!

00:33:45.658 --> 00:33:47.908
He wasn't the person
she intended to poison.

00:33:47.991 --> 00:33:49.658
Huh? Then who?

00:33:49.741 --> 00:33:51.950
We know. That there
was a certain item

00:33:52.033 --> 00:33:54.825
that you desperately wanted to
get back into your possession.

00:33:54.908 --> 00:33:56.783
Even if it meant
killing someone.

00:33:56.866 --> 00:33:58.283
Wait, you mean...

00:33:58.366 --> 00:33:59.741
Ah... Dollie...

00:33:59.825 --> 00:34:00.950
I'm sorry.

00:34:01.033 --> 00:34:02.575
But I'm afraid the one
Dahlia Hawthorne

00:34:02.658 --> 00:34:04.491
was trying to poison...

00:34:04.575 --> 00:34:06.408
...is here.

00:34:06.491 --> 00:34:08.783
Her boyfriend, Phoenix Wright!

00:34:08.866 --> 00:34:09.866
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:34:09.950 --> 00:34:13.658
[wails]

00:34:14.658 --> 00:34:17.325
[PHOENIX]
My sweet Dollie...

00:34:17.408 --> 00:34:20.491
She really... was
trying to kill me?

00:34:20.575 --> 00:34:21.700
Objection!

00:34:21.783 --> 00:34:23.491
Enough with all this poppycock!

00:34:23.575 --> 00:34:25.658
Miss Hawthorne is clearly
in love with this man!

00:34:25.741 --> 00:34:27.658
Yes. Madly in love!

00:34:27.741 --> 00:34:31.450
I'd never hurt my Feenie.
How could you say that?

00:34:31.533 --> 00:34:32.783
It's sick.

00:34:32.866 --> 00:34:35.033
Eight months ago, after
you poisoned that coffee,

00:34:35.116 --> 00:34:37.991
you had yet another
nefarious goal on your mind.

00:34:38.075 --> 00:34:39.533
Getting rid of the evidence.

00:34:39.616 --> 00:34:42.575
The pendant with the poison
bottle had to be disposed of.

00:34:42.658 --> 00:34:44.866
Miss Hawthorne
put her wiles to good use.

00:34:44.950 --> 00:34:47.241
She found someone
who'd gladly take it from her.

00:34:47.325 --> 00:34:48.575
However...

00:34:48.658 --> 00:34:51.283
There was one big problem
she didn't account for.

00:34:51.366 --> 00:34:54.075
Her love-struck mark refused
to give back her "gift."

00:34:54.158 --> 00:34:55.408
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:34:55.491 --> 00:34:58.575
Mister Wright, excuse me,
but have you wondered

00:34:58.658 --> 00:35:00.658
why she fell so hard
for you that day,

00:35:00.741 --> 00:35:02.700
and why you've stayed
together all this time?

00:35:02.783 --> 00:35:04.741
[PHOENIX]
Well, because she...

00:35:04.825 --> 00:35:07.491
[MIA]
She was after something.

00:35:07.575 --> 00:35:08.991
She wanted the pendant back.

00:35:09.075 --> 00:35:10.408
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:35:10.491 --> 00:35:12.741
She got close to you for
that crucial piece of evidence.

00:35:12.825 --> 00:35:15.033
Her "gift" for a man
she didn't know.

00:35:15.116 --> 00:35:16.658
To you, it was a treasure.

00:35:16.741 --> 00:35:17.991
A symbol of true love,

00:35:18.075 --> 00:35:20.741
and something you shared
with anyone who'd look.

00:35:20.825 --> 00:35:22.283
So... you mean...

00:35:22.366 --> 00:35:24.325
The only reason
she dated him was...

00:35:24.408 --> 00:35:27.491
To get it back, even if it
meant she had to murder him.

00:35:27.575 --> 00:35:31.283
[PHOENIX] No. It's because
we were in love, right?

00:35:31.366 --> 00:35:35.575
Ugh. Moron. Would you
get out of the way already?

00:35:35.658 --> 00:35:37.991
Dumb boy, how could
any woman ever count on you

00:35:38.075 --> 00:35:39.658
to take care of things for her?

00:35:39.741 --> 00:35:41.325
I don't know how many times
I told you to keep

00:35:41.408 --> 00:35:43.075
your big mouth shut about me.

00:35:43.158 --> 00:35:44.283
You're worthless!

00:35:44.366 --> 00:35:45.325
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:35:45.408 --> 00:35:46.991
Uh... Witness?

00:35:47.075 --> 00:35:48.908
Ah, I can tell
you plan on making me out

00:35:48.991 --> 00:35:51.033
to be a murderer
no matter what I say.

00:35:51.116 --> 00:35:52.616
You've done it to yourself.

00:35:52.700 --> 00:35:53.866
It's all on you.

00:35:53.950 --> 00:35:57.075
Oh, is it now?
You have nothing concrete on me.

00:35:57.158 --> 00:35:59.741
You're screwed, because
this blubbering little man-child

00:35:59.825 --> 00:36:02.158
took your best piece of
evidence and gobbled it up.

00:36:02.241 --> 00:36:04.825
You have no proof, and you
still have the nerve to treat me

00:36:04.908 --> 00:36:07.158
like I'm some sort of
homicidal maniac?

00:36:07.241 --> 00:36:08.700
I've wasted enough
of my time here,

00:36:08.783 --> 00:36:10.241
so I'll be taking my leave.

00:36:10.325 --> 00:36:11.950
[JUDGE]
Uhh, we're not done yet.

00:36:12.033 --> 00:36:14.700
[DAHLIA] Your Honor. I trust
you'll discipline this nasty,

00:36:14.783 --> 00:36:17.366
overzealous old hag
appropriately, won't you?

00:36:17.450 --> 00:36:19.325
[MIA]
Hold it!

00:36:19.408 --> 00:36:22.241
For what? Did you find
your decisive evidence?

00:36:22.325 --> 00:36:24.783
I refuse to let a person
like you walk free.

00:36:24.866 --> 00:36:26.033
[MARVIN]
Careful, Mia.

00:36:26.116 --> 00:36:27.491
If you keep badgering
the witness like this,

00:36:27.575 --> 00:36:29.991
you could be forced to pay
the ultimate price for it.

00:36:30.075 --> 00:36:32.116
And what do you mean by that?

00:36:32.200 --> 00:36:33.866
He means the penalty
could entail you being

00:36:33.950 --> 00:36:35.700
permanently stripped
of your badge.

00:36:35.783 --> 00:36:37.158
What? Really?

00:36:37.241 --> 00:36:40.491
It's the truth.
You'd be even more washed up.

00:36:40.575 --> 00:36:42.033
[MIA] If I don't back off,
I could be putting

00:36:42.116 --> 00:36:44.533
my career in jeopardy.

00:36:44.616 --> 00:36:48.366
But I swore to fight for
justice and uphold the law.

00:36:48.450 --> 00:36:52.200
What good is this badge if
I abandon the fight so easily?

00:36:52.283 --> 00:36:54.700
Very well. I order
the defense to present

00:36:54.783 --> 00:36:57.033
any evidence it has
against Miss Hawthorne.

00:36:57.116 --> 00:36:58.950
Yes, Your Honor.

00:36:59.033 --> 00:37:00.533
You stupid old cow.

00:37:00.616 --> 00:37:02.450
[MIA] The key to this whole
thing is that poison

00:37:02.533 --> 00:37:05.741
she stole from the lab.
And for me, it's do or die!

00:37:05.825 --> 00:37:07.033
C'mon, Mia!

00:37:07.116 --> 00:37:08.616
[DAHLIA] I've read a
lot of books in my time

00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:10.825
studying literature, but you
going down in flames is

00:37:10.908 --> 00:37:13.533
going to be one of
my favorite stories.

00:37:13.616 --> 00:37:15.033
Maybe I'll write about it.

00:37:15.116 --> 00:37:17.450
I believe in you, Miss Fey.

00:37:17.533 --> 00:37:20.908
There is irrefutable evidence
of Dahlia Hawthorne's crime.

00:37:20.991 --> 00:37:24.533
And I have it. Remember this?

00:37:24.616 --> 00:37:26.158
It's what kills colds dead.

00:37:26.241 --> 00:37:28.700
This bottle of Coldkiller Z
the victim was holding.

00:37:28.783 --> 00:37:30.200
Don't make me laugh.

00:37:30.283 --> 00:37:32.116
That's your "killer" proof, huh?

00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:33.741
Perhaps our rookie
defense lawyer

00:37:33.825 --> 00:37:35.366
isn't feeling well either.

00:37:35.450 --> 00:37:36.783
[MIA]
I'm fine.

00:37:36.866 --> 00:37:39.325
But no matter how I felt,
I wouldn't be taking this.

00:37:39.408 --> 00:37:41.950
Especially not
this particular bottle.

00:37:42.033 --> 00:37:45.116
'Cause this stuff, will
kill more than just a cold.

00:37:45.200 --> 00:37:46.616
[CROWD gasping]

00:37:46.700 --> 00:37:48.366
[PAYNE]
Wait. You think it's poisoned?

00:37:48.450 --> 00:37:49.533
[DAHLIA growls]

00:37:49.616 --> 00:37:52.450
Do you recall the
defendant's testimony?

00:37:52.533 --> 00:37:54.116
[PHOENIX] I'd been trying
to kill this cold with it,

00:37:54.200 --> 00:37:56.825
but I ended up losing the
bottle somewhere that day.

00:37:56.908 --> 00:37:59.783
I could swear I had it
on me till lunchtime, at least.

00:37:59.866 --> 00:38:01.116
Lunchtime.

00:38:01.200 --> 00:38:02.950
That's when Miss Hawthorne
made off with his bottle

00:38:03.033 --> 00:38:04.533
of Coldkiller Z.

00:38:04.616 --> 00:38:06.075
She knew he would take it.

00:38:06.158 --> 00:38:07.741
So she laced it with poison.

00:38:07.825 --> 00:38:09.491
Bunk. Utter claptrap.

00:38:09.575 --> 00:38:11.158
If that's true,
how do you explain

00:38:11.241 --> 00:38:13.158
why the victim
was holding the bottle?

00:38:16.200 --> 00:38:19.491
[MIA] Think back to the crime
that happened eight months ago.

00:38:19.575 --> 00:38:21.991
Where did she hide the
evidence after that went down?

00:38:22.075 --> 00:38:23.616
[JUDGE] And where
would that be, defense?

00:38:23.700 --> 00:38:26.450
[MIA] In that instance, the
poison was inside her pendant.

00:38:26.533 --> 00:38:29.575
Which she made sure to quickly
pass along to someone else.

00:38:29.658 --> 00:38:31.950
The boy she ran
into in the reading room--

00:38:32.033 --> 00:38:34.283
Phoenix Wright.

00:38:34.366 --> 00:38:36.116
She used a
similar tactic in this case

00:38:36.200 --> 00:38:37.491
with Mister Swallow.

00:38:37.575 --> 00:38:39.491
My client says he left
the scene immediately

00:38:39.575 --> 00:38:41.366
after he shoved the victim.

00:38:41.450 --> 00:38:43.283
She had seen
and heard everything.

00:38:43.366 --> 00:38:45.700
The argument,
Mister Swallow's accusation.

00:38:45.783 --> 00:38:47.658
She watched as he was shoved.

00:38:47.741 --> 00:38:51.241
She also saw the
severed electrical cable.

00:38:51.325 --> 00:38:53.575
She realized the victim
would not remain silent

00:38:53.658 --> 00:38:54.825
about her crimes.

00:38:54.908 --> 00:38:57.200
So she decided to use
the cable to guarantee

00:38:57.283 --> 00:38:59.283
he wouldn't tell anybody else.

00:39:00.325 --> 00:39:02.200
[JUDGE] If that's the case,
then what do you make

00:39:02.283 --> 00:39:04.700
of the testimony she
gave the court earlier?

00:39:04.783 --> 00:39:06.616
[MIA] Nothing but
a well-rehearsed lie.

00:39:06.700 --> 00:39:08.200
[PAYNE]
How could she have done it?

00:39:08.283 --> 00:39:10.533
[MIA] Well, she is
a rather frail little thing,

00:39:10.616 --> 00:39:12.616
so it would take her some
time to move Swallow's body

00:39:12.700 --> 00:39:14.075
to where she needed it.

00:39:14.158 --> 00:39:17.158
Which explains the time
discrepancy in the testimony.

00:39:17.241 --> 00:39:19.741
The ten minutes between
the cable falling and his death.

00:39:19.825 --> 00:39:21.908
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:39:21.991 --> 00:39:23.116
At this point.

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.491
Another problem arose
for Miss Hawthorne.

00:39:25.575 --> 00:39:29.200
The defendant, who she'd seen
leaving the scene, came back.

00:39:29.283 --> 00:39:31.116
Also, because
of the power outage,

00:39:31.200 --> 00:39:33.450
the students in the lab
came out to investigate.

00:39:33.533 --> 00:39:35.741
Which caused her to panic.

00:39:35.825 --> 00:39:37.325
After all,

00:39:37.408 --> 00:39:40.200
she was carrying something she
did not want to be caught with.

00:39:40.283 --> 00:39:42.700
The bottle of
poisoned cold medicine.

00:39:42.783 --> 00:39:44.283
The police had
frisked her before,

00:39:44.366 --> 00:39:45.741
what if they did it again?

00:39:45.825 --> 00:39:48.950
It was the same situation
she'd been in the last time.

00:39:49.033 --> 00:39:51.533
And so she did what worked
so well for her eight months

00:39:51.616 --> 00:39:54.950
earlier in the courthouse.
She passed it off.

00:39:55.033 --> 00:39:58.075
And placed it
in the victim's hand!

00:39:58.158 --> 00:40:00.658
[DAHLIA]
Ugh. This is so stupid.

00:40:00.741 --> 00:40:03.533
If you think anybody would
believe this, you're crazy.

00:40:03.616 --> 00:40:04.991
Wouldn't you agree?

00:40:05.075 --> 00:40:06.491
Uh. Yeah.

00:40:06.575 --> 00:40:08.325
The defense has
gotten desperate.

00:40:08.408 --> 00:40:10.658
Don't worry, it's just drivel
and nothing more.

00:40:10.741 --> 00:40:12.241
[MIA]
Objection!

00:40:12.325 --> 00:40:14.741
As a matter of fact,
I feel quite confident.

00:40:14.825 --> 00:40:17.533
However, speaking
of desperation.

00:40:17.616 --> 00:40:19.616
Miss Hawthorne.

00:40:19.700 --> 00:40:21.825
Are you willing to take
this cold medicine?

00:40:21.908 --> 00:40:23.158
[gasps]

00:40:23.241 --> 00:40:25.325
Mister Wright ate
that little pendant of yours.

00:40:25.408 --> 00:40:27.408
Care to do the same with this?

00:40:27.491 --> 00:40:29.658
If it's not poisoned,
then what would be the harm?

00:40:29.741 --> 00:40:31.033
[DAHLIA growls]

00:40:31.116 --> 00:40:32.991
You've testified to the
court about your innocence.

00:40:33.075 --> 00:40:36.325
So, why don't you take
this chance to prove it?

00:40:36.408 --> 00:40:38.116
Right here and now!

00:40:39.908 --> 00:40:46.825
[DAHLIA snarling]

00:40:46.908 --> 00:40:51.575
[DAHLIA, demonic voice]
Mia... Mia...

00:40:51.658 --> 00:40:53.575
Fey...

00:40:53.658 --> 00:40:56.158
Mia Fey!

00:40:56.241 --> 00:40:57.616
[MIA grunts]

00:40:57.700 --> 00:41:00.408
[demonic] Do you believe you
can take me down forever?

00:41:00.491 --> 00:41:04.783
[cackles]

00:41:04.866 --> 00:41:07.408
Okay, fine. You stupid hag.

00:41:07.491 --> 00:41:10.241
Enjoy it while you can.

00:41:10.325 --> 00:41:12.241
[normal voice] I suppose I can
allow you to claim victory

00:41:12.325 --> 00:41:13.408
this time around.

00:41:13.491 --> 00:41:14.741
[gasps]

00:41:14.825 --> 00:41:17.533
Just know... This won't
be the last you see of me.

00:41:17.616 --> 00:41:20.950
You and I will meet again.
Of that, I'm certain.

00:41:21.033 --> 00:41:22.658
I must be going now.

00:41:22.741 --> 00:41:25.116
Off to spend some time
with the boys in blue.

00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:26.741
I wish you the best of luck.

00:41:26.825 --> 00:41:28.033
You'll need it

00:41:29.991 --> 00:41:31.075
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:41:37.408 --> 00:41:39.908
[MIA]
Finally, it's over.

00:41:39.991 --> 00:41:40.741
[banging

00:41:40.825 --> 00:41:41.950
[gasps]

00:41:42.033 --> 00:41:44.283
No, this is a total
miscarriage of justice!

00:41:44.366 --> 00:41:46.700
You failed to present
a drop of proof against her!

00:41:46.783 --> 00:41:48.158
If you believe that...

00:41:48.241 --> 00:41:49.575
I should ask you.

00:41:49.658 --> 00:41:51.783
Would you like to try
a sample of this medicine?

00:41:51.866 --> 00:41:52.950
Huh?

00:41:53.033 --> 00:41:54.200
[MIA] If she's as
innocent as you claim,

00:41:54.283 --> 00:41:56.325
surely, there's nothing
harmful in this bottle.

00:41:56.408 --> 00:41:57.991
It may even clear your sinuses.

00:41:58.075 --> 00:41:59.616
Oh. Well, uh...

00:41:59.700 --> 00:42:01.491
I don't really care
to right now.

00:42:01.575 --> 00:42:03.533
But going off
of what you said earlier,

00:42:03.616 --> 00:42:05.866
I thought you would bet your
very life Miss Hawthorne's word

00:42:05.950 --> 00:42:07.283
was the absolute truth.

00:42:07.366 --> 00:42:09.491
Huh?

00:42:09.575 --> 00:42:10.950
Well, "Rookie Killer"?

00:42:11.033 --> 00:42:13.491
Why don't you show this
rookie how it's really done?

00:42:13.575 --> 00:42:15.616
Do you still abide by
your previous assertion

00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:17.200
of trust in her?

00:42:17.283 --> 00:42:19.783
If you're really willing
to put your life on the line.

00:42:19.866 --> 00:42:21.825
Just how much
is that life worth?

00:42:21.908 --> 00:42:25.491
Please, no!
This can't be happening!

00:42:25.575 --> 00:42:27.116
Not my beautiful pompadour!

00:42:27.200 --> 00:42:29.366
It's flying right off my head!

00:42:29.450 --> 00:42:31.658
[groans]

00:42:31.741 --> 00:42:33.241
Defense.

00:42:33.325 --> 00:42:35.783
I have a sneaking suspicion you
may harbor some sort of grudge

00:42:35.866 --> 00:42:37.325
against Miss Hawthorne.

00:42:37.408 --> 00:42:42.283
[gasps] Your Honor. My feelings
had nothing to do with this.

00:42:42.366 --> 00:42:44.325
Very well, then.

00:42:44.408 --> 00:42:46.991
If there is no further testimony
to be heard today,

00:42:47.075 --> 00:42:48.658
the court is ready to
hand down the verdict

00:42:48.741 --> 00:42:50.158
for Mister Phoenix Wright.

00:42:52.116 --> 00:42:53.408
Not guilty!

00:42:53.491 --> 00:42:56.033
[CROWD cheers]

00:42:56.116 --> 00:42:57.658
[PHOENIX]
Dollie...

00:42:59.408 --> 00:43:01.658
I declare this
court to be adjourned!

00:43:04.033 --> 00:43:06.450
[MARVIN] Great work!
Quite masterfully done!

00:43:06.533 --> 00:43:07.783
I appreciate that.

00:43:07.866 --> 00:43:09.241
Thanks, Mister Grossberg.

00:43:09.325 --> 00:43:11.783
This case really made
me think about something.

00:43:11.866 --> 00:43:14.450
Just how crucial it is to
have a client relationship

00:43:14.533 --> 00:43:16.491
that is built on mutual trust.

00:43:16.575 --> 00:43:19.908
Heh. Congratulations,
Mister Wright.

00:43:19.991 --> 00:43:23.408
You know... I've
been doing some thinking, too.

00:43:23.491 --> 00:43:24.616
About what?

00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:26.116
Was that really her?

00:43:26.200 --> 00:43:28.325
Have I been that
naïve this entire time?

00:43:28.408 --> 00:43:29.116
Huh?

00:43:29.200 --> 00:43:30.700
The girl I loved...

00:43:30.783 --> 00:43:33.200
She would never have said and
done all those terrible things.

00:43:33.283 --> 00:43:36.408
[MIA sighs]

00:43:36.491 --> 00:43:39.533
It's tough, but learn from
this and move on.

00:43:39.616 --> 00:43:42.408
I know. You're right.

00:43:42.491 --> 00:43:43.908
Let me ask you this.

00:43:43.991 --> 00:43:45.408
About your job--

00:43:45.491 --> 00:43:48.533
Lawyers help people out whenever
they're in trouble, right?

00:43:48.616 --> 00:43:50.825
Well, that's my
personal philosophy.

00:43:50.908 --> 00:43:52.283
Nice.

00:43:52.366 --> 00:43:54.700
I've been taking law classes
and it's got me thinking.

00:43:54.783 --> 00:43:57.658
If I become a lawyer
there's a friend I could help.

00:43:57.741 --> 00:43:59.700
After meeting you,
I've made up my mind.

00:43:59.783 --> 00:44:00.741
Oh, really?

00:44:00.825 --> 00:44:02.866
I have! I'll study hard.

00:44:02.950 --> 00:44:06.283
I'm gonna be a lawyer for sure!
And maybe someday--

00:44:06.366 --> 00:44:09.241
You and I will meet again
in the courtroom!

00:44:09.325 --> 00:44:10.950
[MIA]
Hmm. Yeah.

00:44:13.700 --> 00:44:18.658
[heart monitor beeping]

00:44:19.825 --> 00:44:23.616
[MIA] I finally settled the
score for you, like I promised.

00:44:26.533 --> 00:44:27.908
I'll be back.

00:44:35.033 --> 00:44:38.158
[PHOENIX] It's been five years
since that case was closed.

00:44:41.158 --> 00:44:42.658
[PHOENIX]
I did become a lawyer.

00:44:42.741 --> 00:44:44.533
And I even helped my old friend.

00:44:44.616 --> 00:44:49.200
But... Mia's no longer with us.
She's in a better place.

00:44:49.283 --> 00:44:52.741
Even though she's gone,
she's here in other ways.

00:44:52.825 --> 00:44:55.075
And I can always
hear her in my mind.

00:44:55.158 --> 00:44:56.616
[MIA]
Phoenix.

00:44:56.700 --> 00:44:59.283
Remember to always believe in
your client, no matter what.

00:44:59.366 --> 00:45:01.075
The power of that trust
will guide you through

00:45:01.158 --> 00:45:04.325
the toughest cases.
Like a light in the darkness.

00:46:35.408 --> 00:46:36.950
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:46:37.033 --> 00:46:39.283
A broken shell weaves
a tale of memories

00:46:39.366 --> 00:46:41.408
from Mia to Maya to now.

00:46:41.491 --> 00:46:43.200
Little Pearl's journey
through her past

00:46:43.283 --> 00:46:44.741
is about to begin.

00:46:44.825 --> 00:46:48.241
Wait! I can't let her go alone!
I gotta go with her!

00:46:48.325 --> 00:46:50.491
Look for a new shell,
solve the mystery,

00:46:50.575 --> 00:46:52.408
and carve a path to the future!

00:46:52.491 --> 00:46:54.575
For the first time,
Pearl and I are gonna have

00:46:54.658 --> 00:46:56.991
an adventure together.
Let's hit the road!

00:46:57.075 --> 00:46:59.491
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:46:59.575 --> 00:47:01.866
Next Episode: "Hear the
Waves of Turnabout!"

00:47:01.950 --> 00:47:03.241
Take that!
